== digits_that_are_no_colour
note: 27 rows with NA in educ or wage dropped (line 2)
note: 35 rows with NA in educ, wage or hours dropped (line 3)
error[Z0401]: `fill:` of `scale` is "#12", which is not a colour: after `#` come six hexadecimal digits, or three
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:15
  |
4 | p.scale(fill: ["grey", "#12"])
  |               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ not six hexadecimal digits, or three
  |
  = help: write the red, the green and the blue as two digits each, as in "#4682B4"; "#48B" is short for "#4488BB"

