== a_size_of_zero
note: 27 rows with NA in educ or wage dropped (line 2)
note: 35 rows with NA in educ, wage or hours dropped (line 3)
error[Z0401]: a size of `scale` is the diameter of a mark, in points, above 0, but this is 0
 --> scripts/main.zeff:4:15
  |
4 | p.scale(size: [0, 4])
  |               ^^^^^^ not the sizes of a scale
  |
  = help: write the diameter of the largest mark, in points, as in `scale(size: [24])`, where a size shows an amount by its area; or those of the marks of the smallest and of the largest value, as in `scale(size: [2, 12])`, where it shows a difference

